<article class="env-definition" id="6A779E">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/6A779E">Definition <span data-tag="6A779E">1.1.5.3</span>.</a> Let $f: J \rightarrow J'$ be a monotone map between linearly ordered sets. The simplicial functor $\sCoNerve [f]: \sCoNerve [\Delta ^ J] \rightarrow \sCoNerve [\Delta ^{J'}]$ is defined as follows: </p>
  <p><ul>
  <li><p>
For each object $i \in \sCoNerve [\Delta ^ J]$, $\sCoNerve [f](i) = f(i) \in \sCoNerve [\Delta ^{J'}]$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
If $i \leq j$ in $J$, then the map $ \bHom _{\sCoNerve [\Delta ^ J]}(i,j) \rightarrow \bHom _{\sCoNerve [\Delta ^{J'}]}(f(i),f(j))$ induced by $f$ is the nerve of the map 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[ P_{i,j} \rightarrow P_{f(i),f(j)} \]
</div>
<div class="equation">
  \[  I \mapsto f(I). \]
</div>
</li>
</ul></p>
</article>